    "dismal": {
      "word": "DISMAL",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "Fatal; ill-omened; unlucky. [Obs.] An ugly fiend more foul than dismal day. Spenser.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gloomy to the eye or ear; sorrowful and depressing to the feelings; foreboding; cheerless; dull; dreary; as, a dismal outlook; dismal stories; a dismal place. Full well the busy whisper, circling round, Convey'd the dismal tidings when he frowned. Goldsmith. A dismal description of an English November. Southey. doleful; lugubrious; funereal; dolorous; calamitous; sorrowful; sad; joyless; melancholy; unfortunate; unhappy.",
          "partOfSpeech": "adjective"
        }
      ],
