    "dismay": {
      "word": "DISMAY",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "To take dismay or fright; to be filled with dismay. [Obs.] Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "Loss of courage and firmness through fear; overwhelming and disabling terror; a sinking of the spirits; consternation. I . . . can not think of such a battle without dismay. Macaulay. Thou with a tiger spring dost leap upon thy prey, And tear his helpless breast, o'erwhelmed with wild dismay. Mrs. Barbauld.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Condition fitted to dismay; ruin. Spenser. apprehension; alarm; affright.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
